WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.966
Gaining a Deeper Understanding of Defect Opportunities

2
00:00:04.966 --> 00:00:10.832
Hello, Mike Harry and welcome back. Where we’re looking at the idea of defect opportunities

3
00:00:10.833 --> 00:00:14.266
and how that plays out in the world of Six Sigma.

4
00:00:14.266 --> 00:00:21.066
Now, at the very root of every transaction or process

5
00:00:21.066 --> 00:00:25.499
or product. Be it service, industrial, commercial doesn’t matter.

6
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:30.766
At the node level, at the base, is an opportunity.

7
00:00:30.766 --> 00:00:36.899
And of course, an opportunity is a set of circumstances that is favorable to an end.

8
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:43.433
And we put the word defect in front of it, we’re saying it's a set of circumstances, conditions,

9
00:00:43.433 --> 00:00:50.299
that is favorable to the formation of a defect, an error, a fault. Whatever you want to call it.

10
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:54.300
It's an opportunity for something to go wrong.

11
00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:59.566
Of course we have opportunities for things to go right, but again semantics.

12
00:00:59.566 --> 00:01:02.932
Whether it goes right or whether it goes wrong, heads and tails,

13
00:01:02.933 --> 00:01:05.899
different sides of the same coin.

14
00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:09.833
And in this segment because the counting of opportunities

15
00:01:09.833 --> 00:01:15.333
and understanding what an opportunity is, is at the root of how we reason through Six Sigma.

16
00:01:15.333 --> 00:01:20.733
See, Six Sigma applies at the opportunity level of a product or service.

17
00:01:20.733 --> 00:01:27.066
And understanding that, is essential to better understanding Six Sigma.

18
00:01:27.066 --> 00:01:32.066
Thank you for choosing SSMI.
